{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RvLhXBVfbW7WRjiwa3jVdA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n3\t\"\"\"check-installer-write-safety.py — PLAN-185 W0, 5th pass (FAIL-CLOSED DISCOVERY).\n4\t\n5\tCensus of two classes of unsafe write in ``scripts/**/*.sh``:\n6\t\n7\t  symlink-follow  a path is decided by a DEREFERENCING file test (-e/-f/-d/...,\n8\t                  anything but -L/-h) and is also WRITTEN.  Both a dangling and\n9\t                  a resolved symlink at that path make the write land OUTSIDE\n10\t                  the tree the installer was given.  (CWE-59 / CWE-61)\n11\t\n12\t  sed-interp      an operator-controlled value is interpolated into a sed/awk\n13\t                  substitution without escaping that substitution's delimiter\n14\t                  (and & / backslash on the replacement side).  The value\n15\t                  aborts the command; because ``>`` created the destination\n16\t                  first, the abort leaves a 0-byte file that the EXISTS-skip\n17\t                  branch then treats as installed forever.\n18\t\n19\tWHY THIS FILE WAS REWRITTEN TWICE (verdict, then DISCOVERY)\n20\t-----------------------------------------------------------\n21\tPasses 1..3 worked by *implicit denylist*: they enumerated the syntactic forms\n22\tthey could recognise and credited ``guardado``/``nao-aplicavel`` to everything\n23\tthat did not match.  Every form nobody thought of was born fail-OPEN, so every\n24\treview round found more of them — 8, then 7, then 9, then 10, then 16.\n25\t\n26\tThe 4th pass inverted the VERDICT rule: safety became a THEOREM provable only\n27\tby a named form in ALLOWLIST below.  The 5th round of review then returned 16\n28\tfindings of the SAME class, because inverting the verdict is only half the\n29\tjob.  DISCOVERY was still a denylist: a site existed only where a recognised\n30\tfile test or a bare ``sed`` name appeared, so ``test -a \"$dst\"``,\n31\t``/usr/bin/sed``, ``$1``, ``>& \"$dst\"`` and ``sort -o \"$dst\"`` produced no site\n32\tAT ALL.  An invisible site is worse than a wrongly-cleared one: nothing in the\n33\toutput says it exists.\n34\t\n35\tThis pass makes discovery fail-closed as well.  A command is PROVEN read-only\n36\tonly if its name is in PROVEN_READONLY and it opens no file for output;\n37\teverything else whose operands or redirections carry an expansion is a\n38\tCANDIDATE WRITE (class ``write-candidate``) that must be proven safe like any\n39\tother site.  A test expression the model cannot walk to the end, an\n40\t``eval``/``source``/``exec``, and an unparseable file are sites too.  The\n41\tcensus therefore reports what it does NOT understand, which is the only way a\n42\t\"no finding\" line can mean anything.\n43\t\n44\tThree structural consequences, all deliberate:\n45\t\n46\t0. **Volume went up ~5x, and that is the correct direction.**  The baseline is\n47\t   a RATCHET over what the instrument can see, not a list of reviewed defects;\n48\t   PLAN-185 W1/W2 is what turns real sites into ``guardado``.  A small baseline\n49\t   here would only mean discovery was narrow again.\n50\t\n51\t1. **Reachability analysis is gone.**  The old matcher spent ~600 lines asking\n52\t   \"is the write reachable when the link dangles?\", and answered\n53\t   ``nao-aplicavel`` whenever it could not tell.  That question was wrong on\n54\t   its own terms: the threat model covers the RESOLVED link too (``-e`` true,\n55\t   ``cp`` writes through it, clobbering a file outside the target), so the\n56\t   branch a dangling link happens to take never decided safety.  An argument\n57\t   about control flow can only make a site MORE dangerous, never safe, so no\n58\t   such argument can produce a non-blocking verdict here.  Safety comes from a\n59\t   dominating ``-L`` guard or from there being no write at all — nothing else.\n60\t\n61\t2. **Parsing is fail-closed.**  Analysis runs on a real (small) shell lexer and\n62\t   a block-scope stack, not on regexes over raw text.  Unbalanced quotes, an\n63\t   unterminated heredoc, a block stack that does not close, an unreadable file\n64\t   — any of these makes the WHOLE FILE unparseable: it emits a synthetic\n65\t   blocking ``parse`` site and every site inside it is ``indeterminado``.\n66\t\n67\tSITE CLASSES\n68\t------------\n69\t  symlink-follow  a dereferencing file test decides a path that is written.\n70\t  sed-interp      a value is interpolated into a stream-editor script.\n71\t  write-candidate a command that is not PROVEN read-only touches an expansion.\n72\t  parse           the file could not be read or modelled at all.\n73\t\n74\tVERDICTS\n75\t--------\n76\t  nao-aplicavel   PROVEN: nothing writes the tested path (form a3 / n0).\n77\t  guardado        PROVEN: a non-dereferencing guard dominates every write\n78\t                  (forms a1, a2), or the interpolation is provably escaped or\n79\t                  validated (forms b1, b2, b3).\n80\t  desguardado     PROVEN dangerous: a write exists with no dominating guard,\n81\t                  or a raw interpolation with no escaping anywhere.\n82\t  indeterminado   NOT PROVEN either way.  Blocks.\n83\t\n84\tBoth ``desguardado`` and ``indeterminado`` are BLOCKING and must appear in the\n85\ttracked baseline.  Being in the baseline means a human LOOKED — never that the\n86\tform is tolerated.\n87\t\n88\tEXIT CODES\n89\t----------\n90\t  0  every blocking site is recorded in the baseline and every baseline entry\n91\t     still matches a site.\n92\t  1  drift: a blocking site is missing from the baseline, or a baseline entry\n93\t     matches nothing (rot), or --strict is on and any site is indeterminate.\n94\t  2  the census found ZERO sites.  This FAILS by design: zero means the search\n95\t     is broken, not that the corpus is clean.\n96\t\n97\tPython >= 3.9, stdlib only.\n98\t\"\"\"\n99\t\n100\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n101\t\n102\timport argparse\n103\timport hashlib\n104\timport json\n105\timport os\n106\timport re\n107\timport sys\n108\tfrom pathlib import Path\n109\tfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Sequence, Set, Tuple\n110\t\n111\t_INSTRUMENT_PACKAGE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n112\t_REPO_ROOT = next(\n113\t    (ancestor.parent for ancestor in _INSTRUMENT_PACKAGE.parents\n114\t     if ancestor.name == \".claude\" and (ancestor / \"scripts\").is_dir()),\n115\t    Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3],\n116\t)\n117\t\n118\t\n119\tdef instrument_sha256() -> str:\n120\t    \"\"\"Digest the entry point and every shipped implementation component.\n121\t\n122\t    A census number published without it is not reproducible: the same corpus\n123\t    judged by two versions of this script is two different measurements, and\n124\t    this instrument has changed under a reader at least once.\n125\t    \"\"\"\n126\t    try:\n127\t        package = _INSTRUMENT_PACKAGE\n128\t        entry_point = package.parent / \"check-installer-write-safety.py\"\n129\t        if not entry_point.is_file():\n130\t            entry_point = package.parents[2] / \"scripts\" / \"check-installer-write-safety.py\"\n131\t        members = [entry_point] + sorted(package.glob(\"*.py\"))\n132\t        digest = hashlib.sha256()\n133\t        for member in members:\n134\t            payload = member.read_bytes()\n135\t            name = (\"entry/\" + member.name if member == entry_point\n136\t                    else \"package/\" + member.name)\n137\t            digest.update(name.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n138\t            digest.update(b\"\\x00\")\n139\t            digest.update(str(len(payload)).encode(\"ascii\"))\n140\t            digest.update(b\"\\x00\")\n141\t            digest.update(payload)\n142\t            digest.update(b\"\\x00\")\n143\t        return digest.hexdigest()\n144\t    except OSError:\n145\t        return \"unavailable\"\n146\t\n147\tDEFAULT_SCAN_ROOT = \"scripts\"\n148\tDEFAULT_BASELINE_REL = \".claude/scripts/data/installer-write-safety-baseline.txt\"\n149\tEXCLUDED_REL_PREFIXES = (\"scripts/tests/\",)\n150\t\n151\tCLASS_SYMLINK = \"symlink-follow\"\n152\tCLASS_SED = \"sed-interp\"\n153\tCLASS_PARSE = \"parse\"\n154\t# Fail-closed DISCOVERY (5th pass).  A command that is not PROVEN read-only and\n155\t# touches an expansion is a candidate write, whether or not anything ever\n156\t# tested that path.  Without this class the census could only see writes that\n157\t# some `-e`/`-f` test had already pointed at, so the forms nobody tested were\n158\t# invisible rather than indeterminate.\n159\tCLASS_WRITE = \"write-candidate\"\n160\t\n161\tVERDICT_GUARDED = \"guardado\"\n162\tVERDICT_UNGUARDED = \"desguardado\"\n163\tVERDICT_INDETERMINATE = \"indeterminado\"\n164\tVERDICT_NA = \"nao-aplicavel\"\n165\t\n166\tBLOCKING_VERDICTS = (VERDICT_UNGUARDED, VERDICT_INDETERMINATE)\n167\t\n168\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n169\t# THE ALLOWLIST.  A site may leave the blocking set ONLY through one of these\n170\t# named forms.  Each id is asserted by a positive control in\n171\t# .claude/scripts/tests/test_check_installer_write_safety.py: the form with its\n172\t# guard present must come out non-blocking, and the same fixture with the guard\n173\t# removed or mutated must come out blocking, naming the path.\n174\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n175\tALLOWLIST = (\n176\t    (\"a1-nofollow-test-dominates\",\n177\t     \"A -L/-h test on the same path, whose taken branch aborts at the branch's \"\n178\t     \"own level, on an earlier logical line whose scope path is a prefix of \"\n179\t     \"every write's scope path.\"),\n180\t    (\"a2-nofollow-helper-dominates\",\n181\t     \"A call to a helper DEFINED IN THE SAME FILE whose body satisfies a1 for \"\n182\t     \"$1 and whose symlink branch returns a NON-ZERO literal, called as \"\n183\t     \"`helper <path> || <abort>` (or aborting the process outright).  The \"\n184\t     \"helper's body is inspected; its NAME is never evidence.\"),\n185\t    (\"a3-no-write-to-operand\",\n186\t     \"Every occurrence of the tested path (and of its one-level aliases) in the \"\n187\t     \"analysis region is at a position proven not to write: a file test, an \"\n188\t     \"argument of a PROVEN_READONLY command, a read redirection, or the SOURCE \"\n189\t     \"operand of a known writer.  A single occurrence the model cannot place \"\n190\t     \"voids the proof.\"),\n191\t    (\"a4-confinement-predicate-dominates\",\n192\t     \"A dominating call to a predicate DEFINED EXACTLY ONCE in the scanned \"\n193\t     \"corpus -- another file is fine -- whose BODY applies a \"\n194\t     \"non-dereferencing check to a path built from its own positional \"\n195\t     \"parameters and has an explicit refusal path, called in a modelled \"\n196\t     \"refusal polarity, AND whose arguments COVER the write destination: \"\n197\t     \"either the destination itself or the (root, relpath) pair it is \"\n198\t     \"concatenated from.  Cross-file resolution never credits a NAME -- an \"\n199\t     \"ambiguous or missing definition fails, and so does an argument list \"\n200\t     \"that does not bind the destination.\"),\n201\t    (\"b1-delimiter-escape-dominates\",\n202\t     \"Every assignment to the interpolated variable in the region escapes the \"\n203\t     \"delimiter OF THIS SUBSTITUTION (plus & and backslash on the replacement \"\n204\t     \"side) with a replacement that actually inserts a backslash, and at least \"\n205\t     \"one of those assignments dominates the use.\"),\n206\t    (\"b2-closed-charset-validated\",\n207\t     \"A dominating validation aborts unless the value matches a literal closed \"\n208\t     \"character class that excludes this substitution's delimiter, &, \"\n209\t     \"backslash and newline.\"),\n210\t    (\"b3-literal-only\",\n211\t     \"The substitution contains no expansion at all, or every assignment to the \"\n212\t     \"interpolated variable in the region is a literal free of the delimiter, \"\n213\t     \"& and backslash.\"),\n214\t    (\"b4-inline-escape-substitution\",\n215\t     \"The interpolation is a single command substitution that escapes THIS \"\n216\t     \"substitution's delimiter in place (plus & and backslash), with a \"\n217\t     \"replacement that actually inserts a backslash.\"),\n218\t    (\"n0-no-interpolation\",\n219\t     \"The stream-editor invocation's script is fully literal and contains no \"\n220\t     \"substitution with an expansion in it.\"),\n221\t)\n222\tALLOWLIST_IDS = frozenset(i for i, _ in ALLOWLIST)\n223\t\n224\t# Reason codes attached to indeterminate verdicts.  Every one of them means\n225\t# \"the model does not cover this shape\", never \"this looked fine\".\n226\tR_PARSE = \"i-parse-failed\"\n227\tR_UNREADABLE = \"i-file-unreadable\"\n228\tR_OCCURRENCE = \"i-unmodeled-occurrence\"\n229\tR_GUARD_NOT_DOM = \"i-guard-not-dominating\"\n230\tR_SCRIPT_DYNAMIC = \"i-script-not-literal\"\n231\tR_SCRIPT_UNPARSED = \"i-script-unparsed\"\n232\tR_CMD_SUBST = \"i-command-substitution\"\n233\tR_ESCAPE_UNPROVEN = \"i-escape-unproven\"\n234\tR_AWK_EXPANSION = \"i-awk-program-interpolated\"\n235\tR_GUARD_STALE = \"i-guard-value-rebound\"\n236\tR_TEST_UNMODELED = \"i-unmodeled-test-form\"\n237\tR_CANDIDATE = \"i-write-candidate-unproven\"\n238\tR_OPAQUE = \"i-opaque-command\"\n239\tR_PRED_AMBIGUOUS = \"i-predicate-definition-ambiguous\"\n240\tR_PRED_ARG_UNBOUND = \"i-predicate-arg-unbound\"\n241\t\n242\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n243\t# Lexer\n244\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n245\t\n246\t\n247\t\n248\t__all__ = [name for name in globals() if not name.startswith(\"__\")]\n249\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9f21750-77cd-44a8-9a48-5376b7294476","uuid":"4cb0e6e6-835c-48f5-93ac-635bed766b9f","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:58:29.580Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/_installer_write_safety/engine.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"check-installer-write-safety.py — PLAN-185 W0, 5th pass (FAIL-CLOSED DISCOVERY).\n\nCensus of two classes of unsafe write in ``scripts/**/*.sh``:\n\n  symlink-follow  a path is decided by a DEREFERENCING file test (-e/-f/-d/...,\n                  anything but -L/-h) and is also WRITTEN.  Both a dangling and\n                  a resolved symlink at that path make the write land OUTSIDE\n                  the tree the installer was given.  (CWE-59 / CWE-61)\n\n  sed-interp      an operator-controlled value is interpolated into a sed/awk\n                  substitution without escaping that substitution's delimiter\n                  (and & / backslash on the replacement side).  The value\n                  aborts the command; because ``>`` created the destination\n                  first, the abort leaves a 0-byte file that the EXISTS-skip\n                  branch then treats as installed forever.\n\nWHY THIS FILE WAS REWRITTEN TWICE (verdict, then DISCOVERY)\n-----------------------------------------------------------\nPasses 1..3 worked by *implicit denylist*: they enumerated the syntactic forms\nthey could recognise and credited ``guardado``/``nao-aplicavel`` to everything\nthat did not match.  Every form nobody thought of was born fail-OPEN, so every\nreview round found more of them — 8, then 7, then 9, then 10, then 16.\n\nThe 4th pass inverted the VERDICT rule: safety became a THEOREM provable only\nby a named form in ALLOWLIST below.  The 5th round of review then returned 16\nfindings of the SAME class, because inverting the verdict is only half the\njob.  DISCOVERY was still a denylist: a site existed only where a recognised\nfile test or a bare ``sed`` name appeared, so ``test -a \"$dst\"``,\n``/usr/bin/sed``, ``$1``, ``>& \"$dst\"`` and ``sort -o \"$dst\"`` produced no site\nAT ALL.  An invisible site is worse than a wrongly-cleared one: nothing in the\noutput says it exists.\n\nThis pass makes discovery fail-closed as well.  A command is PROVEN read-only\nonly if its name is in PROVEN_READONLY and it opens no file for output;\neverything else whose operands or redirections carry an expansion is a\nCANDIDATE WRITE (class ``write-candidate``) that must be proven safe like any\nother site.  A test expression the model cannot walk to the end, an\n``eval``/``source``/``exec``, and an unparseable file are sites too.  The\ncensus therefore reports what it does NOT understand, which is the only way a\n\"no finding\" line can mean anything.\n\nThree structural consequences, all deliberate:\n\n0. **Volume went up ~5x, and that is the correct direction.**  The baseline is\n   a RATCHET over what the instrument can see, not a list of reviewed defects;\n   PLAN-185 W1/W2 is what turns real sites into ``guardado``.  A small baseline\n   here would only mean discovery was narrow again.\n\n1. **Reachability analysis is gone.**  The old matcher spent ~600 lines asking\n   \"is the write reachable when the link dangles?\", and answered\n   ``nao-aplicavel`` whenever it could not tell.  That question was wrong on\n   its own terms: the threat model covers the RESOLVED link too (``-e`` true,\n   ``cp`` writes through it, clobbering a file outside the target), so the\n   branch a dangling link happens to take never decided safety.  An argument\n   about control flow can only make a site MORE dangerous, never safe, so no\n   such argument can produce a non-blocking verdict here.  Safety comes from a\n   dominating ``-L`` guard or from there being no write at all — nothing else.\n\n2. **Parsing is fail-closed.**  Analysis runs on a real (small) shell lexer and\n   a block-scope stack, not on regexes over raw text.  Unbalanced quotes, an\n   unterminated heredoc, a block stack that does not close, an unreadable file\n   — any of these makes the WHOLE FILE unparseable: it emits a synthetic\n   blocking ``parse`` site and every site inside it is ``indeterminado``.\n\nSITE CLASSES\n------------\n  symlink-follow  a dereferencing file test decides a path that is written.\n  sed-interp      a value is interpolated into a stream-editor script.\n  write-candidate a command that is not PROVEN read-only touches an expansion.\n  parse           the file could not be read or modelled at all.\n\nVERDICTS\n--------\n  nao-aplicavel   PROVEN: nothing writes the tested path (form a3 / n0).\n  guardado        PROVEN: a non-dereferencing guard dominates every write\n                  (forms a1, a2), or the interpolation is provably escaped or\n                  validated (forms b1, b2, b3).\n  desguardado     PROVEN dangerous: a write exists with no dominating guard,\n                  or a raw interpolation with no escaping anywhere.\n  indeterminado   NOT PROVEN either way.  Blocks.\n\nBoth ``desguardado`` and ``indeterminado`` are BLOCKING and must appear in the\ntracked baseline.  Being in the baseline means a human LOOKED — never that the\nform is tolerated.\n\nEXIT CODES\n----------\n  0  every blocking site is recorded in the baseline and every baseline entry\n     still matches a site.\n  1  drift: a blocking site is missing from the baseline, or a baseline entry\n     matches nothing (rot), or --strict is on and any site is indeterminate.\n  2  the census found ZERO sites.  This FAILS by design: zero means the search\n     is broken, not that the corpus is clean.\n\nPython >= 3.9, stdlib only.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Sequence, Set, Tuple\n\n_INSTRUMENT_PACKAGE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n_REPO_ROOT = next(\n    (ancestor.parent for ancestor in _INSTRUMENT_PACKAGE.parents\n     if ancestor.name == \".claude\" and (ancestor / \"scripts\").is_dir()),\n    Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3],\n)\n\n\ndef instrument_sha256() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Digest the entry point and every shipped implementation component.\n\n    A census number published without it is not reproducible: the same corpus\n    judged by two versions of this script is two different measurements, and\n    this instrument has changed under a reader at least once.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        package = _INSTRUMENT_PACKAGE\n        entry_point = package.parent / \"check-installer-write-safety.py\"\n        if not entry_point.is_file():\n            entry_point = package.parents[2] / \"scripts\" / \"check-installer-write-safety.py\"\n        members = [entry_point] + sorted(package.glob(\"*.py\"))\n        digest = hashlib.sha256()\n        for member in members:\n            payload = member.read_bytes()\n            name = (\"entry/\" + member.name if member == entry_point\n                    else \"package/\" + member.name)\n            digest.update(name.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n            digest.update(b\"\\x00\")\n            digest.update(str(len(payload)).encode(\"ascii\"))\n            digest.update(b\"\\x00\")\n            digest.update(payload)\n            digest.update(b\"\\x00\")\n        return digest.hexdigest()\n    except OSError:\n        return \"unavailable\"\n\nDEFAULT_SCAN_ROOT = \"scripts\"\nDEFAULT_BASELINE_REL = \".claude/scripts/data/installer-write-safety-baseline.txt\"\nEXCLUDED_REL_PREFIXES = (\"scripts/tests/\",)\n\nCLASS_SYMLINK = \"symlink-follow\"\nCLASS_SED = \"sed-interp\"\nCLASS_PARSE = \"parse\"\n# Fail-closed DISCOVERY (5th pass).  A command that is not PROVEN read-only and\n# touches an expansion is a candidate write, whether or not anything ever\n# tested that path.  Without this class the census could only see writes that\n# some `-e`/`-f` test had already pointed at, so the forms nobody tested were\n# invisible rather than indeterminate.\nCLASS_WRITE = \"write-candidate\"\n\nVERDICT_GUARDED = \"guardado\"\nVERDICT_UNGUARDED = \"desguardado\"\nVERDICT_INDETERMINATE = \"indeterminado\"\nVERDICT_NA = \"nao-aplicavel\"\n\nBLOCKING_VERDICTS = (VERDICT_UNGUARDED, VERDICT_INDETERMINATE)\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# THE ALLOWLIST.  A site may leave the blocking set ONLY through one of these\n# named forms.  Each id is asserted by a positive control in\n# .claude/scripts/tests/test_check_installer_write_safety.py: the form with its\n# guard present must come out non-blocking, and the same fixture with the guard\n# removed or mutated must come out blocking, naming the path.\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nALLOWLIST = (\n    (\"a1-nofollow-test-dominates\",\n     \"A -L/-h test on the same path, whose taken branch aborts at the branch's \"\n     \"own level, on an earlier logical line whose scope path is a prefix of \"\n     \"every write's scope path.\"),\n    (\"a2-nofollow-helper-dominates\",\n     \"A call to a helper DEFINED IN THE SAME FILE whose body satisfies a1 for \"\n     \"$1 and whose symlink branch returns a NON-ZERO literal, called as \"\n     \"`helper <path> || <abort>` (or aborting the process outright).  The \"\n     \"helper's body is inspected; its NAME is never evidence.\"),\n    (\"a3-no-write-to-operand\",\n     \"Every occurrence of the tested path (and of its one-level aliases) in the \"\n     \"analysis region is at a position proven not to write: a file test, an \"\n     \"argument of a PROVEN_READONLY command, a read redirection, or the SOURCE \"\n     \"operand of a known writer.  A single occurrence the model cannot place \"\n     \"voids the proof.\"),\n    (\"a4-confinement-predicate-dominates\",\n     \"A dominating call to a predicate DEFINED EXACTLY ONCE in the scanned \"\n     \"corpus -- another file is fine -- whose BODY applies a \"\n     \"non-dereferencing check to a path built from its own positional \"\n     \"parameters and has an explicit refusal path, called in a modelled \"\n     \"refusal polarity, AND whose arguments COVER the write destination: \"\n     \"either the destination itself or the (root, relpath) pair it is \"\n     \"concatenated from.  Cross-file resolution never credits a NAME -- an \"\n     \"ambiguous or missing definition fails, and so does an argument list \"\n     \"that does not bind the destination.\"),\n    (\"b1-delimiter-escape-dominates\",\n     \"Every assignment to the interpolated variable in the region escapes the \"\n     \"delimiter OF THIS SUBSTITUTION (plus & and backslash on the replacement \"\n     \"side) with a replacement that actually inserts a backslash, and at least \"\n     \"one of those assignments dominates the use.\"),\n    (\"b2-closed-charset-validated\",\n     \"A dominating validation aborts unless the value matches a literal closed \"\n     \"character class that excludes this substitution's delimiter, &, \"\n     \"backslash and newline.\"),\n    (\"b3-literal-only\",\n     \"The substitution contains no expansion at all, or every assignment to the \"\n     \"interpolated variable in the region is a literal free of the delimiter, \"\n     \"& and backslash.\"),\n    (\"b4-inline-escape-substitution\",\n     \"The interpolation is a single command substitution that escapes THIS \"\n     \"substitution's delimiter in place (plus & and backslash), with a \"\n     \"replacement that actually inserts a backslash.\"),\n    (\"n0-no-interpolation\",\n     \"The stream-editor invocation's script is fully literal and contains no \"\n     \"substitution with an expansion in it.\"),\n)\nALLOWLIST_IDS = frozenset(i for i, _ in ALLOWLIST)\n\n# Reason codes attached to indeterminate verdicts.  Every one of them means\n# \"the model does not cover this shape\", never \"this looked fine\".\nR_PARSE = \"i-parse-failed\"\nR_UNREADABLE = \"i-file-unreadable\"\nR_OCCURRENCE = \"i-unmodeled-occurrence\"\nR_GUARD_NOT_DOM = \"i-guard-not-dominating\"\nR_SCRIPT_DYNAMIC = \"i-script-not-literal\"\nR_SCRIPT_UNPARSED = \"i-script-unparsed\"\nR_CMD_SUBST = \"i-command-substitution\"\nR_ESCAPE_UNPROVEN = \"i-escape-unproven\"\nR_AWK_EXPANSION = \"i-awk-program-interpolated\"\nR_GUARD_STALE = \"i-guard-value-rebound\"\nR_TEST_UNMODELED = \"i-unmodeled-test-form\"\nR_CANDIDATE = \"i-write-candidate-unproven\"\nR_OPAQUE = \"i-opaque-command\"\nR_PRED_AMBIGUOUS = \"i-predicate-definition-ambiguous\"\nR_PRED_ARG_UNBOUND = \"i-predicate-arg-unbound\"\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Lexer\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n__all__ = [name for name in globals() if not name.startswith(\"__\")]\n","numLines":249,"startLine":1,"totalLines":249}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RvLhXBVfbW7WRjiwa3jVdA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
