ck is the applied one).\n    None when there is none or the inventory cannot be read (fail-open: the\n    caller falls back to the generator's own answer).\"\"\"\n    pinned = read_codex_pin(repo).get(\"package_version\")\n    if pinned == version:\n        return None\n    try:\n        want = tool.parse_version(version)\n        rows = tool.mold_inventory(repo)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — infra fail-open; newest_mold() names it\n        return None\n    hits = sorted(r[\"rel\"] for r in rows if r.get(\"target\") == want)\n    return hits[-1] if hits else None\n\n\ndef _stale_pack_reason(tool: Any, repo: Path, mold_rel: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"Why an existing constants-block pack can no longer be applied, or None.\n\n    That grammar records the sha256 of the live pin and manifest when the\n    pack was generated (``BASE_PIN_SHA256``/``BASE_MAN_SHA256``) and its\n    ceremony dies when either file changed since. A heredoc-grammar pack\n    records neither, and a mold this generator does not parse is not judged\n    (fail-open: the caller keeps the \"apply the existing pack\" advice).\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        text = (repo / mold_rel).read_bytes().decode(\"utf-8\")\n        parts = tool.parse_mold(text)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — infra/unparsed mold: not judged\n        return None\n    if parts.get(\"grammar\") != getattr(tool, \"GRAMMAR_CONSTANTS\", None):\n        return None\n    consts = parts.get(\"consts\") or {}\n    changed = []\n    for key, rel in ((\"BASE_PIN_SHA256\", tool.PIN_REL), (\"BASE_MAN_SHA256\", tool.MANIFEST_REL)):\n        entry = consts.get(key)\n        if entry is None:\n            return None\n        try:\n            live = hashlib.sha256((repo / rel).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n        except OSError:\n            return None\n        if entry[1].strip(\"'\") != live:\n            changed.append(rel)\n    if not changed:\n        return None\n    return \"{} changed after the pack was generated (its {} no longer match)\".format(\n        \" and \".join(changed), \"BASE_*_SHA256\" if len(changed) > 1 else \"BASE_* sha256\")\n\n\ndef _codex_installed_findings(repo: Path, pin: Dict[str, Any],\n                              installed: str) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    pinned = pin[\"package_version\"]\n    clauses = parse_range(pin[\"range\"]) if pin.get(\"range\") else None\n    range_note = \"\"\n    if clauses is not None:\n        range_note = \" (pre-flight range {}: {})\".format(\n            pin[\"range\"], \"inside\" if in_range(installed, clauses) else \"OUTSIDE\")\n    if installed == pinned:\n        if clauses is not None and not in_range(pinned, clauses):\n            return [_finding(\"codex\", \"CODEX_PIN_PACK_INCOHERENT\", \"drift\",\n                             \"manifest pins {} but codex-cli-pin.txt range {} excludes it\".format(\n                                 pinned, pin[\"range\"]), repin_next(repo, pinned))]\n        return []\n    if (clauses is not None and len(clauses) == 1 and clauses[0][0] == \">=\"\n            and _RELEASE_RE.match(installed) and in_range(installed, clauses)):\n        return [_finding(\n            \"codex\", \"CODEX_INSTALLED_COMPATIBLE\", \"info\",\n            \"installed codex {} meets the unbounded semantic floor {} — version \"\n            \"compatibility only; the payload hash is verified separately\".format(\n                installed, pin[\"range\"]),\n            [], {\"installed\": installed, \"floor\": pin[\"range\"]})]\n    ikey, pkey = semver_key(installed), semver_key(pinned)\n    claim = (\"installed codex {} is not the pinned {}{} — the payload sha256 will not \"\n             \"match the manifest, so the pair-rail fails CLOSED at the next L3+ call\"\n             ).format(installed, pinned, range_note)\n    if (ikey is not None and pkey is not None and ikey < pkey) or not _RELEASE_RE.match(installed):\n        # Older than the pin, or a prerelease (never re-pinned): restore.\n        nxt = [\"npm i -g {}@{}   # Owner-run: restore the pinned binary\".format(\n            _NPM_PACKAGE, pinned),\n            \"python3 .claude/hooks/check_pair_rail.py --verify-codex-pin\"]\n    else:\n        nxt = repin_next(repo, installed) + [\n            \"or restore the pinned binary (Owner-run): npm i -g {}@{}\".format(\n                _NPM_PACKAGE, pinned)]\n    return [_finding(\"codex\", \"CODEX_INSTALLED_NOT_PINNED\", \"drift\", claim, nxt,\n                     {\"installed\": installed, \"pinned\": pinned})]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# npm dist-tags cache (the ONLY network path; opt-in)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef default_cache_path(repo: Path, project: Optional[str]) -> Optional[Path]:\n    \"\"\"Cache under the project runtime state dir — the single resolver.\n\n    ``project`` None keeps the resolver's own precedence (CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR,\n    else cwd); an explicit --repo-root is passed AS GIVEN (no realpath: the\n    harness slugs the launch path as given — runtime_paths \"symlink honesty\").\n    \"\"\"\n    hooks = repo / \".claude\" / \"hooks\"\n    candidates = [hooks, SCRIPT_DIR.parent / \"hooks\"]\n    for cand in candidates:\n        if (cand / \"_lib\" / \"runtime_paths.py\").is_file():\n            if str(cand) not in sys.path:\n                sys.path.insert(0, str(cand))\n            break\n    try:\n        from _lib import runtime_paths as _rp  # noqa: E402\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — infra fail-open\n        return None\n    return _rp.runtime_state_dir(project=project) / _CACHE_SUBDIR / _CACHE_NAME\n\n\ndef validate_dist_tags(obj: Any) -> Optional[Dict[str, str]]:\n    \"\"\"Untrusted data: keep only tag -> strict-semver pairs (first 256).\n\n    Entries of any other shape are DROPPED, never echoed; the result is None\n    (unusable) unless a strict-semver ``latest`` survives — the one tag the\n    upstream check reads.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(obj, dict):\n        return None\n    tags: Dict[str, str] = {}\n    for key, val in list(obj.items())[:256]:\n        if isinstance(key, str) and _TAG_KEY_RE.match(key) and \\\n                isinstance(val, str) and _SEMVER_FULL_RE.match(val):\n            tags[key] = val\n    return tags if \"latest\" in tags else None\n\n\ndef _atomic_write_json(path: Path, payload: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True, mode=0o700)\n    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=\".tmp-\", dir=str(path.parent))\n    try:\n        with os.fdopen(fd, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            json.dump(payload, fh, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n            fh.write(\"\\n\")\n        os.replace(tmp, str(path))\n    except BaseException:\n        try:\n            os.unlink(tmp)\n        except OSError:","numLines":170,"startLine":480,"totalLines":1285}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015c2XUttSN87pZzSR1mubjJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7CYiX51wVioAy4CU7h8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NiXw26etzcCPrqfRsjUjer","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/scripts/check-substrate-watch.py","offset":1,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9144,"cache_read_input_tokens":120145,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9144},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9f21750-77cd-44a8-9a48-5376b7294476","uuid":"6b30d370-b250-4dc9-bb99-4d3f217951b9","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:59:35.058Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7CYiJRhxT2TJ9hTra1k","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NiXw26etzcCPrqfRsjUjer":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/scripts/check-substrate-watch.py","offset":1,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NiXw26etzcCPrqfRsjUjer","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"check-substrate-watch.py — Claude Code + Agent-SDK substrate drift watch.\n3\t\n4\tPLAN-135 W5 unit o8o11o12 (O12). The heroic manual changelog sweeps (S214,\n5\tS230, and THIS plan's 8-dimension research pass) became a permanent nightly\n6\tinstrument: a small read-only checker that compares the substrate version this\n7\tframework was last RECONCILED against (`.claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json`\n8\t`last_seen`) with the version actually installed locally — and surfaces the\n9\tfetch-the-upstream-changelog step as a PENDING-OWNER recipe (agents stay\n10\tno-network under ADR-136-AMEND-1; the doc fetch costs no model tokens but is\n11\tthe one network action, so it is Owner-run by design).\n12\t\n13\tA newer upstream/installed version is NOT a defect: it is a prompt to re-run\n14\tverify-the-knob-routes before trusting an assumption baked against an older\n15\tsurface (the S217/S228 silent-knob class). Detection only; never a BREAK.\n16\t\n17\tSemantics:\n18\t  - `last_seen.version == \"unknown\"` OR `_meta.source_stale == true`\n19\t      -> status \"stale-ledger\" (advisory): the ledger has never been Owner\n20\t         -refreshed against the live changelog. ONE finding, disposition=defer.\n21\t  - a code-registered probe (selected by the component's `key`, see\n22\t    `_PROBE_ARGV`) resolves an installed version that differs from\n23\t    `last_seen.version` -> status \"drift\": ONE finding per component\n24\t    (disposition=fix-or-defer; claim names old vs installed).\n25\t  - everything matches and the ledger is fresh -> status \"current\".\n26\t\n27\tProbing is OPT-IN (`--probe-installed`): by default the checker does NOT run\n28\tany version command (zero side effects, suitable for the read-only nightly\n29\tagent which then reports the ledger state + recipe). With `--probe-installed`\n30\tit runs each component's CODE-DEFINED read-only version probe — the argv is\n31\thardcoded in `_PROBE_ARGV`, keyed on the component `key`; the ledger can NEVER\n32\tsupply a command (Codex R2 P0) — with a short timeout and fail-soft.\n33\t\n34\tExit codes:\n35\t  0 — report mode (always), or --check with a fresh ledger + no drift,\n36\t      or infra fail-open (missing/corrupt ledger: advisory + exit 0)\n37\t  1 — --check only: ledger stale OR drift detected (a maintenance signal,\n38\t      not infra failure)\n39\t  2 — CLI usage error (argparse)\n40\t\n41\tPLAN-155 Wave 0 (debate A12) extended coverage to the Codex HOST-harness\n42\tsubstrate: the `codex_harness` ledger entry watches the codex-cli release\n43\tfeed AND the developers.openai.com/codex/{hooks,config-reference,rules} doc\n44\tpages; both codex-keyed components now carry a code-defined version probe\n45\t(`codex --version`), and a detected codex drift attaches the code-registered\n46\tfixture re-record runbook (`_DRIFT_RUNBOOKS`): bump the pin via the ADR-111\n47\tceremony FIRST, then re-record the Wave-1 adapter fixtures.\n48\t\n49\tStdlib-only. Python >= 3.9. Read-only (never writes; --refresh only PRINTS\n50\tthe recipe, it does not fetch). Emits NO audit events.\n51\t\"\"\"\n52\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n53\t\n54\timport argparse\n55\timport json\n56\timport os\n57\timport re\n58\timport subprocess  # nosec B404 — read-only version probes, opt-in, fail-soft\n59\timport sys\n60\tfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n61\t\n62\tSCRIPT_DIR = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\n63\tHOOKS_DIR = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, \"..\", \"hooks\"))\n64\tif HOOKS_DIR not in sys.path:\n65\t    sys.path.insert(0, HOOKS_DIR)\n66\t\n67\tfrom _lib import cli_currency  # noqa: E402\n68\t\n69\tDEFAULT_LEDGER_PATH = os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, \"substrate-watch.json\")\n70\t\n71\t_VERSION_RE = re.compile(r\"(\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+(?:[-.][0-9A-Za-z.\\-]+)?)\")\n72\t_PROBE_TIMEOUT_S = 8.0\n73\t\n74\t# Closed registry of version probes (PLAN-135 Codex R1/R2 P0). The full argv for\n75\t# each component — INCLUDING any `-e`/`-c` interpreter payload — is hardcoded HERE,\n76\t# keyed on the component's `key`. The ledger (and `--ledger <file>`) can only\n77\t# SELECT a key; it can NEVER supply the command. This closes the RCE class\n78\t# completely: an allowlist of argv[0] is insufficient because `python3`/`node`/\n79\t# `npx` are themselves arbitrary-code-execution vectors (`python3 -c <evil>`).\n80\t# Unknown key -> no probe. The ledger's descriptive `local_probe` (if present)\n81\t# is intentionally NOT executed; it is human documentation only.\n82\t_PROBE_ARGV: Dict[str, List[str]] = {\n83\t    \"claude_code\": [\"claude\", \"--version\"],\n84\t    \"agent_sdk_ts\": [\n85\t        \"node\", \"-e\",\n86\t        \"console.log(require('@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk/package.json').version)\",\n87\t    ],\n88\t    \"agent_sdk_py\": [\n89\t        \"python3\", \"-c\",\n90\t        \"import importlib.metadata as m; print(m.version('claude-agent-sdk'))\",\n91\t    ],\n92\t    # PLAN-155 Wave 0 (debate A12): the Codex substrate is watched by TWO\n93\t    # ledger entries backed by the SAME read-only binary probe — `codex_cli`\n94\t    # (pair-rail reviewer flag-surface, PLAN-142 lineage; previously had no\n95\t    # probe registered) and `codex_harness` (Codex-as-HOST hooks/config/rules\n96\t    # schema surface, PLAN-155).\n97\t    \"codex_cli\": [\"codex\", \"--version\"],\n98\t    \"codex_harness\": [\"codex\", \"--version\"],\n99\t    # PLAN-178 W1.2-5c (codex S306 r5 P2 cure): the native per-agent usage\n100\t    # source is a shape OF the Claude Code harness — its installed version IS\n101\t    # the harness version, so a harness bump marks this component drifted and\n102\t    # triggers the promised native-shape re-fingerprint.\n103\t    \"cc_native_usage\": [\"claude\", \"--version\"],\n104\t}\n105\t\n106\t# Code-registered drift runbooks (PLAN-155 Wave 0, debate A12). Same posture\n107\t# as _PROBE_ARGV (Codex R2 P0): the ledger can only SELECT a component key —\n108\t# it can NEVER supply alert/procedure text of its own. When a component with\n109\t# a registered runbook drifts, the runbook is attached to that report row\n110\t# (`runbook`) and printed in text mode, so the alert names the exact\n111\t# re-record procedure instead of a bare version delta.\n112\t_CODEX_FIXTURE_RUNBOOK = (\n113\t    \"codex-cli drift — fixture re-record runbook (PLAN-155 debate A12): do \"\n114\t    \"NOT re-record fixtures against the new binary directly. (1) bump the \"\n115\t    \"pin FIRST via the ADR-182 pin ceremony (codex-cli-pin.txt semver range \"\n116\t    \"+ codex-cli-pin-manifest.json per-triple PAYLOAD sha256 — the retired \"\n117\t    \"codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt launcher hash is a tombstone); (2) THEN \"\n118\t    \"re-record the PLAN-155 Wave-1 \"\n119\t    \"host-adapter fixtures under .claude/hooks/tests/fixtures/adapters/codex/ \"\n120\t    \"(each fixture carries _meta.codex_cli_version; the pin-range test stays \"\n121\t    \"RED until fixtures are re-recorded or explicitly waived); (3) run the \"\n122\t    \"per-bump re-verification checklist in ADR-161 (hook envelope schema, \"\n123\t    \"PreToolUse interception surface, /hooks trust-hash keying, SubagentStart \"\n124\t    \"continue:false, Stop decision:block, execpolicy prefix_rule syntax).\"\n125\t)\n126\t_DRIFT_RUNBOOKS: Dict[str, str] = {\n127\t    \"codex_cli\": _CODEX_FIXTURE_RUNBOOK,\n128\t    \"codex_harness\": _CODEX_FIXTURE_RUNBOOK,\n129\t}\n130\t\n131\t\n132\tdef load_ledger(path: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n133\t    \"\"\"Read the substrate-watch ledger. None on any failure (fail-open).\"\"\"\n134\t    try:\n135\t        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n136\t            data = json.load(fh)\n137\t        if not isinstance(data, dict):\n138\t            return None\n139\t        return data\n140\t    except (OSError, ValueError):\n141\t        return None\n142\t\n143\t\n144\tdef _extract_version(text: str) -> Optional[str]:\n145\t    \"\"\"First semver-ish token in `text` (e.g. 'claude 1.2.3 (...)' -> '1.2.3').\"\"\"\n146\t    match = _VERSION_RE.search(text or \"\")\n147\t    return match.group(1) if match else None\n148\t\n149\t\n150\tdef _run_version_cmd(argv: List[str]) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:\n151\t    \"\"\"Execute a registered version probe (shell=False). Test seam — unit tests\n152\t    patch THIS symbol to script probe output without touching a real binary.\"\"\"\n153\t    return subprocess.run(  # nosec B603 — fixed argv from _PROBE_ARGV (code-defined, NOT ledger-controlled)\n154\t        argv,\n155\t        shell=False,\n156\t        capture_output=True,\n157\t        text=True,\n158\t        timeout=_PROBE_TIMEOUT_S,\n159\t    )\n160\t\n161\t\n162\tdef _probe_installed(key: str) -> Tuple[Optional[str], str]:\n163\t    \"\"\"Resolve the installed version for component ``key`` via its code-defined\n164\t    probe in ``_PROBE_ARGV``. Returns (version|None, note).\n165\t\n166\t    The command is NEVER taken from ledger data (Codex R2 P0) — only the key\n167\t    selects which hardcoded argv runs. Fail-soft: an unregistered key, missing\n168\t    binary, non-zero exit, timeout, or unparseable output all degrade to\n169\t    (None, <reason>) — never raises.\n170\t    \"\"\"\n171\t    argv = _PROBE_ARGV.get(key)\n172\t    if not argv:\n173\t        return None, \"no probe registered for component %r\" % key\n174\t    try:\n175\t        proc = _run_version_cmd(argv)\n176\t    except (subprocess.TimeoutExpired, OSError) as exc:\n177\t        return None, \"probe unavailable (%s)\" % type(exc).__name__\n178\t    if proc.returncode != 0:\n179\t        return None, \"probe exit %d (not installed?)\" % proc.returncode\n180\t    version = _extract_version((proc.stdout or \"\") + \" \" + (proc.stderr or \"\"))\n181\t    if version is None:\n182\t        return None, \"probe ran but no version token parsed\"\n183\t    return version, \"ok\"\n184\t\n185\t\n186\tdef build_report(\n187\t    ledger: Optional[Dict[str, Any]],\n188\t    *,\n189\t    probe_installed: bool = False,\n190\t) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n191\t    \"\"\"Pure-ish builder (the only impurity is the opt-in version probe).\n192\t\n193\t    Returns a dict with: status, summary, source_stale, components[].\n194\t    NEVER raises.\n195\t    \"\"\"\n196\t    if ledger is None:\n197\t        return {\n198\t            \"schema\": 1,\n199\t            \"fail_open\": True,\n200\t            \"status\": \"current\",\n201\t            \"summary\": \"substrate-watch ledger missing/corrupt — advisory, \"\n202\t            \"treated as no-drift (run from the repo root; the ledger ships at \"\n203\t            \".claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json)\",\n204\t            \"source_stale\": False,\n205\t            \"components\": [],\n206\t        }\n207\t\n208\t    meta = ledger.get(\"_meta\") if isinstance(ledger.get(\"_meta\"), dict) else {}\n209\t    source_stale = bool(meta.get(\"source_stale\", False))\n210\t    components_in = ledger.get(\"components\")\n211\t    components_in = components_in if isinstance(components_in, list) else []\n212\t\n213\t    rows: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n214\t    any_drift = False\n215\t    any_unknown = False\n216\t    for comp in components_in:\n217\t        if not isinstance(comp, dict):\n218\t            continue\n219\t        last_seen = comp.get(\"last_seen\") if isinstance(comp.get(\"last_seen\"), dict) else {}\n220\t        seen_version = str(last_seen.get(\"version\", \"unknown\"))\n221\t        row: Dict[str, Any] = {\n222\t            \"key\": comp.get(\"key\", \"?\"),\n223\t            \"label\": comp.get(\"label\", comp.get(\"key\", \"?\")),\n224\t            \"last_seen_version\": seen_version,\n225\t            \"last_seen_date\": str(last_seen.get(\"date\", \"unknown\")),\n226\t            \"installed_version\": None,\n227\t            \"probe_note\": \"not probed (--probe-installed off)\",\n228\t            \"drift\": False,\n229\t            \"runbook\": None,\n230\t        }\n231\t        if seen_version == \"unknown\":\n232\t            any_unknown = True\n233\t        if probe_installed:\n234\t            installed, note = _probe_installed(str(comp.get(\"key\", \"\")))\n235\t            row[\"installed_version\"] = installed\n236\t            row[\"probe_note\"] = note\n237\t            codex_current = (\n238\t                str(comp.get(\"key\", \"\")) in (\"codex_cli\", \"codex_harness\")\n239\t                and cli_currency.compare_semver(\n240\t                    installed, cli_currency.CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR\n241\t                ) is not None\n242\t                and cli_currency.compare_semver(\n243\t                    installed, cli_currency.CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR\n244\t                ) >= 0\n245\t            )\n246\t            if installed is not None and codex_current:\n247\t                row[\"currency\"] = \"compatible\"\n248\t            elif installed is not None and seen_version != \"unknown\" and installed != seen_version:\n249\t                row[\"drift\"] = True\n250\t                any_drift = True\n251\t                # Attach the code-registered runbook (None-safe): the alert\n252\t                # names the fixture re-record procedure, not just the delta.\n253\t                row[\"runbook\"] = _DRIFT_RUNBOOKS.get(str(comp.get(\"key\", \"\")))\n254\t        rows.append(row)\n255\t\n256\t    if source_stale or any_unknown:\n257\t        status = \"stale-ledger\"\n258\t        summary = (\n259\t            \"substrate-watch ledger never Owner-refreshed against the live \"\n260\t            \"changelog (source_stale or last_seen=unknown) — PENDING-OWNER: %s\"\n261\t            % str(meta.get(\"refresh_recipe\", \"run --refresh for the recipe\"))\n262\t        )\n263\t    elif any_drift:\n264\t        status = \"drift\"\n265\t        drifted = [r[\"key\"] for r in rows if r[\"drift\"]]\n266\t        summary = \"installed substrate differs from last-reconciled for: %s\" % drifted\n267\t    else:\n268\t        status = \"current\"\n269\t        summary = \"substrate reconciled — installed matches last_seen for all components\"\n270\t\n271\t    return {\n272\t        \"schema\": 1,\n273\t        \"fail_open\": False,\n274\t        \"status\": status,\n275\t        \"summary\": summary,\n276\t        \"source_stale\": source_stale,\n277\t        \"components\": rows,\n278\t    }\n279\t\n280\t\n281\t_REFRESH_RECIPE = \"\"\"\\\n282\tPENDING-OWNER substrate-watch refresh (no model tokens; one doc fetch each):\n283\t  For each component in .claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json:\n284\t    1. WebFetch the _meta.sources value for that key. A STRING is one\n285\t       URL; a LIST means fetch EACH URL in it (PLAN-155 A12: e.g.\n286\t       codex_harness = release feed + the three host-harness doc pages).\n287\t    2. Single-URL key: read the topmost version + release date on the\n288\t       page. LIST key: last_seen.version tracks the versioned feed (the\n289\t       first URL); the doc pages carry no version — record last_seen.date\n290\t       as the newest visible 'last updated' across ALL pages, and treat\n291\t       ANY observed change on a doc page as drift for that component\n292\t       EVEN IF the release feed shows no new version (docs-only schema\n293\t       drift is exactly the class this entry watches; on drift follow\n294\t       the component's registered runbook in _DRIFT_RUNBOOKS).\n295\t    3. Set components[key].last_seen.version + .date to those values.\n296\t    4. Set _meta.fetched to today and _meta.source_stale to false.\n297\t  This is Owner-run by design — the nightly agent stays no-network\n298\t  (ADR-136-AMEND-1). The fetch bills no model tokens; record nothing\n299\t  billable. After it lands, dimension vii reports 'current' until the\n300\t  next upstream release.\"\"\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9f21750-77cd-44a8-9a48-5376b7294476","uuid":"e0b1dd98-a92f-474d-a48d-cefda47517c3","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:59:35.068Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/scripts/check-substrate-watch.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"check-substrate-watch.py — Claude Code + Agent-SDK substrate drift watch.\n\nPLAN-135 W5 unit o8o11o12 (O12). The heroic manual changelog sweeps (S214,\nS230, and THIS plan's 8-dimension research pass) became a permanent nightly\ninstrument: a small read-only checker that compares the substrate version this\nframework was last RECONCILED against (`.claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json`\n`last_seen`) with the version actually installed locally — and surfaces the\nfetch-the-upstream-changelog step as a PENDING-OWNER recipe (agents stay\nno-network under ADR-136-AMEND-1; the doc fetch costs no model tokens but is\nthe one network action, so it is Owner-run by design).\n\nA newer upstream/installed version is NOT a defect: it is a prompt to re-run\nverify-the-knob-routes before trusting an assumption baked against an older\nsurface (the S217/S228 silent-knob class). Detection only; never a BREAK.\n\nSemantics:\n  - `last_seen.version == \"unknown\"` OR `_meta.source_stale == true`\n      -> status \"stale-ledger\" (advisory): the ledger has never been Owner\n         -refreshed against the live changelog. ONE finding, disposition=defer.\n  - a code-registered probe (selected by the component's `key`, see\n    `_PROBE_ARGV`) resolves an installed version that differs from\n    `last_seen.version` -> status \"drift\": ONE finding per component\n    (disposition=fix-or-defer; claim names old vs installed).\n  - everything matches and the ledger is fresh -> status \"current\".\n\nProbing is OPT-IN (`--probe-installed`): by default the checker does NOT run\nany version command (zero side effects, suitable for the read-only nightly\nagent which then reports the ledger state + recipe). With `--probe-installed`\nit runs each component's CODE-DEFINED read-only version probe — the argv is\nhardcoded in `_PROBE_ARGV`, keyed on the component `key`; the ledger can NEVER\nsupply a command (Codex R2 P0) — with a short timeout and fail-soft.\n\nExit codes:\n  0 — report mode (always), or --check with a fresh ledger + no drift,\n      or infra fail-open (missing/corrupt ledger: advisory + exit 0)\n  1 — --check only: ledger stale OR drift detected (a maintenance signal,\n      not infra failure)\n  2 — CLI usage error (argparse)\n\nPLAN-155 Wave 0 (debate A12) extended coverage to the Codex HOST-harness\nsubstrate: the `codex_harness` ledger entry watches the codex-cli release\nfeed AND the developers.openai.com/codex/{hooks,config-reference,rules} doc\npages; both codex-keyed components now carry a code-defined version probe\n(`codex --version`), and a detected codex drift attaches the code-registered\nfixture re-record runbook (`_DRIFT_RUNBOOKS`): bump the pin via the ADR-111\nceremony FIRST, then re-record the Wave-1 adapter fixtures.\n\nStdlib-only. Python >= 3.9. Read-only (never writes; --refresh only PRINTS\nthe recipe, it does not fetch). Emits NO audit events.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport subprocess  # nosec B404 — read-only version probes, opt-in, fail-soft\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\nSCRIPT_DIR = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\nHOOKS_DIR = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, \"..\", \"hooks\"))\nif HOOKS_DIR not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, HOOKS_DIR)\n\nfrom _lib import cli_currency  # noqa: E402\n\nDEFAULT_LEDGER_PATH = os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, \"substrate-watch.json\")\n\n_VERSION_RE = re.compile(r\"(\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+(?:[-.][0-9A-Za-z.\\-]+)?)\")\n_PROBE_TIMEOUT_S = 8.0\n\n# Closed registry of version probes (PLAN-135 Codex R1/R2 P0). The full argv for\n# each component — INCLUDING any `-e`/`-c` interpreter payload — is hardcoded HERE,\n# keyed on the component's `key`. The ledger (and `--ledger <file>`) can only\n# SELECT a key; it can NEVER supply the command. This closes the RCE class\n# completely: an allowlist of argv[0] is insufficient because `python3`/`node`/\n# `npx` are themselves arbitrary-code-execution vectors (`python3 -c <evil>`).\n# Unknown key -> no probe. The ledger's descriptive `local_probe` (if present)\n# is intentionally NOT executed; it is human documentation only.\n_PROBE_ARGV: Dict[str, List[str]] = {\n    \"claude_code\": [\"claude\", \"--version\"],\n    \"agent_sdk_ts\": [\n        \"node\", \"-e\",\n        \"console.log(require('@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk/package.json').version)\",\n    ],\n    \"agent_sdk_py\": [\n        \"python3\", \"-c\",\n        \"import importlib.metadata as m; print(m.version('claude-agent-sdk'))\",\n    ],\n    # PLAN-155 Wave 0 (debate A12): the Codex substrate is watched by TWO\n    # ledger entries backed by the SAME read-only binary probe — `codex_cli`\n    # (pair-rail reviewer flag-surface, PLAN-142 lineage; previously had no\n    # probe registered) and `codex_harness` (Codex-as-HOST hooks/config/rules\n    # schema surface, PLAN-155).\n    \"codex_cli\": [\"codex\", \"--version\"],\n    \"codex_harness\": [\"codex\", \"--version\"],\n    # PLAN-178 W1.2-5c (codex S306 r5 P2 cure): the native per-agent usage\n    # source is a shape OF the Claude Code harness — its installed version IS\n    # the harness version, so a harness bump marks this component drifted and\n    # triggers the promised native-shape re-fingerprint.\n    \"cc_native_usage\": [\"claude\", \"--version\"],\n}\n\n# Code-registered drift runbooks (PLAN-155 Wave 0, debate A12). Same posture\n# as _PROBE_ARGV (Codex R2 P0): the ledger can only SELECT a component key —\n# it can NEVER supply alert/procedure text of its own. When a component with\n# a registered runbook drifts, the runbook is attached to that report row\n# (`runbook`) and printed in text mode, so the alert names the exact\n# re-record procedure instead of a bare version delta.\n_CODEX_FIXTURE_RUNBOOK = (\n    \"codex-cli drift — fixture re-record runbook (PLAN-155 debate A12): do \"\n    \"NOT re-record fixtures against the new binary directly. (1) bump the \"\n    \"pin FIRST via the ADR-182 pin ceremony (codex-cli-pin.txt semver range \"\n    \"+ codex-cli-pin-manifest.json per-triple PAYLOAD sha256 — the retired \"\n    \"codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt launcher hash is a tombstone); (2) THEN \"\n    \"re-record the PLAN-155 Wave-1 \"\n    \"host-adapter fixtures under .claude/hooks/tests/fixtures/adapters/codex/ \"\n    \"(each fixture carries _meta.codex_cli_version; the pin-range test stays \"\n    \"RED until fixtures are re-recorded or explicitly waived); (3) run the \"\n    \"per-bump re-verification checklist in ADR-161 (hook envelope schema, \"\n    \"PreToolUse interception surface, /hooks trust-hash keying, SubagentStart \"\n    \"continue:false, Stop decision:block, execpolicy prefix_rule syntax).\"\n)\n_DRIFT_RUNBOOKS: Dict[str, str] = {\n    \"codex_cli\": _CODEX_FIXTURE_RUNBOOK,\n    \"codex_harness\": _CODEX_FIXTURE_RUNBOOK,\n}\n\n\ndef load_ledger(path: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Read the substrate-watch ledger. None on any failure (fail-open).\"\"\"\n    try:\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            data = json.load(fh)\n        if not isinstance(data, dict):\n            return None\n        return data\n    except (OSError, ValueError):\n        return None\n\n\ndef _extract_version(text: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"First semver-ish token in `text` (e.g. 'claude 1.2.3 (...)' -> '1.2.3').\"\"\"\n    match = _VERSION_RE.search(text or \"\")\n    return match.group(1) if match else None\n\n\ndef _run_version_cmd(argv: List[str]) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:\n    \"\"\"Execute a registered version probe (shell=False). Test seam — unit tests\n    patch THIS symbol to script probe output without touching a real binary.\"\"\"\n    return subprocess.run(  # nosec B603 — fixed argv from _PROBE_ARGV (code-defined, NOT ledger-controlled)\n        argv,\n        shell=False,\n        capture_output=True,\n        text=True,\n        timeout=_PROBE_TIMEOUT_S,\n    )\n\n\ndef _probe_installed(key: str) -> Tuple[Optional[str], str]:\n    \"\"\"Resolve the installed version for component ``key`` via its code-defined\n    probe in ``_PROBE_ARGV``. Returns (version|None, note).\n\n    The command is NEVER taken from ledger data (Codex R2 P0) — only the key\n    selects which hardcoded argv runs. Fail-soft: an unregistered key, missing\n    binary, non-zero exit, timeout, or unparseable output all degrade to\n    (None, <reason>) — never raises.\n    \"\"\"\n    argv = _PROBE_ARGV.get(key)\n    if not argv:\n        return None, \"no probe registered for component %r\" % key\n    try:\n        proc = _run_version_cmd(argv)\n    except (subprocess.TimeoutExpired, OSError) as exc:\n        return None, \"probe unavailable (%s)\" % type(exc).__name__\n    if proc.returncode != 0:\n        return None, \"probe exit %d (not installed?)\" % proc.returncode\n    version = _extract_version((proc.stdout or \"\") + \" \" + (proc.stderr or \"\"))\n    if version is None:\n        return None, \"probe ran but no version token parsed\"\n    return version, \"ok\"\n\n\ndef build_report(\n    ledger: Optional[Dict[str, Any]],\n    *,\n    probe_installed: bool = False,\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Pure-ish builder (the only impurity is the opt-in version probe).\n\n    Returns a dict with: status, summary, source_stale, components[].\n    NEVER raises.\n    \"\"\"\n    if ledger is None:\n        return {\n            \"schema\": 1,\n            \"fail_open\": True,\n            \"status\": \"current\",\n            \"summary\": \"substrate-watch ledger missing/corrupt — advisory, \"\n            \"treated as no-drift (run from the repo root; the ledger ships at \"\n            \".claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json)\",\n            \"source_stale\": False,\n            \"components\": [],\n        }\n\n    meta = ledger.get(\"_meta\") if isinstance(ledger.get(\"_meta\"), dict) else {}\n    source_stale = bool(meta.get(\"source_stale\", False))\n    components_in = ledger.get(\"components\")\n    components_in = components_in if isinstance(components_in, list) else []\n\n    rows: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n    any_drift = False\n    any_unknown = False\n    for comp in components_in:\n        if not isinstance(comp, dict):\n            continue\n        last_seen = comp.get(\"last_seen\") if isinstance(comp.get(\"last_seen\"), dict) else {}\n        seen_version = str(last_seen.get(\"version\", \"unknown\"))\n        row: Dict[str, Any] = {\n            \"key\": comp.get(\"key\", \"?\"),\n            \"label\": comp.get(\"label\", comp.get(\"key\", \"?\")),\n            \"last_seen_version\": seen_version,\n            \"last_seen_date\": str(last_seen.get(\"date\", \"unknown\")),\n            \"installed_version\": None,\n            \"probe_note\": \"not probed (--probe-installed off)\",\n            \"drift\": False,\n            \"runbook\": None,\n        }\n        if seen_version == \"unknown\":\n            any_unknown = True\n        if probe_installed:\n            installed, note = _probe_installed(str(comp.get(\"key\", \"\")))\n            row[\"installed_version\"] = installed\n            row[\"probe_note\"] = note\n            codex_current = (\n                str(comp.get(\"key\", \"\")) in (\"codex_cli\", \"codex_harness\")\n                and cli_currency.compare_semver(\n                    installed, cli_currency.CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR\n                ) is not None\n                and cli_currency.compare_semver(\n                    installed, cli_currency.CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR\n                ) >= 0\n            )\n            if installed is not None and codex_current:\n                row[\"currency\"] = \"compatible\"\n            elif installed is not None and seen_version != \"unknown\" and installed != seen_version:\n                row[\"drift\"] = True\n                any_drift = True\n                # Attach the code-registered runbook (None-safe): the alert\n                # names the fixture re-record procedure, not just the delta.\n                row[\"runbook\"] = _DRIFT_RUNBOOKS.get(str(comp.get(\"key\", \"\")))\n        rows.append(row)\n\n    if source_stale or any_unknown:\n        status = \"stale-ledger\"\n        summary = (\n            \"substrate-watch ledger never Owner-refreshed against the live \"\n            \"changelog (source_stale or last_seen=unknown) — PENDING-OWNER: %s\"\n            % str(meta.get(\"refresh_recipe\", \"run --refresh for the recipe\"))\n        )\n    elif any_drift:\n        status = \"drift\"\n        drifted = [r[\"key\"] for r in rows if r[\"drift\"]]\n        summary = \"installed substrate differs from last-reconciled for: %s\" % drifted\n    else:\n        status = \"current\"\n        summary = \"substrate reconciled — installed matches last_seen for all components\"\n\n    return {\n        \"schema\": 1,\n        \"fail_open\": False,\n        \"status\": status,\n        \"summary\": summary,\n        \"source_stale\": source_stale,\n        \"components\": rows,\n    }\n\n\n_REFRESH_RECIPE = \"\"\"\\\nPENDING-OWNER substrate-watch refresh (no model tokens; one doc fetch each):\n  For each component in .claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json:\n    1. WebFetch the _meta.sources value for that key. A STRING is one\n       URL; a LIST means fetch EACH URL in it (PLAN-155 A12: e.g.\n       codex_harness = release feed + the three host-harness doc pages).\n    2. Single-URL key: read the topmost version + release date on the\n       page. LIST key: last_seen.version tracks the versioned feed (the\n       first URL); the doc pages carry no version — record last_seen.date\n       as the newest visible 'last updated' across ALL pages, and treat\n       ANY observed change on a doc page as drift for that component\n       EVEN IF the release feed shows no new version (docs-only schema\n       drift is exactly the class this entry watches; on drift follow\n       the component's registered runbook in _DRIFT_RUNBOOKS).\n    3. Set components[key].last_seen.version + .date to those values.\n    4. Set _meta.fetched to today and _meta.source_stale to false.\n  This is Owner-run by design — the nightly agent stays no-network\n  (ADR-136-AMEND-1). The fetch bills no model tokens; record nothing\n  billable. After it lands, dimension vii reports 'current' until the\n  next upstream release.\"\"\"","numLines":300,"startLine":1,"totalLines":359}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NiXw26etzcCPrqfRsjUjer","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
