r-rail on the 0.139 CLI surface. The binary-SHA pin\n# (codex-cli-binary-sha256.txt -> d3be844c...) remains the real supply-chain\n# gate; this semver range is the pair-rail-gate.sh pre-flight message. Per\n# ADR-111 the 0.128->0.139 jump runs the locked-corpus catch_rate check\n# (Owner elected to RUN it this ceremony, not defer) — see PLAN-142 §4.\n#\n# PLAN-156 update (S269 2026-07-12, SENT-CX-PIN): widened upper bound to\n# <0.145.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.144.1 is in-range — the\n# bump that restores frontier-model access (GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra/Luna are\n# first-class from 0.143.0; 0.139 cannot run them). LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED\n# at >=0.128.0 (debate C10 / pair-rail R2: raising it would drop an\n# in-flight RC verdict out of range in release.yml step-15 and red-lock a\n# GA cut — widen-upper-only is the ONLY safe shape during any release\n# window; this bump was executed OUTSIDE an open release window).\n# Empirical base: PLAN-156/artifacts/characterization-grok-codex-S269.md\n# (0.144.1 flag surface verified — the 0.139 verified-compose\n# `exec --color never --sandbox <mode> -o <file> --output-schema --json -m`\n# is UNCHANGED; sandbox enum still read-only|workspace-write|\n# danger-full-access; reasoning-effort accepts max/xhigh client-side;\n# 0.144.0 open bugs #31873/#31860/#31826 triaged non-blocking, #31869\n# CLOSED upstream 2026-07-10). Locked-corpus catch_rate check: Owner\n# elects run-vs-defer at SENT-CX-PIN signing (S246 precedent: run it).\n#\n# PLAN-174 update (S318 2026-08-20, pack SENT-S318): widened upper bound to\n# <0.148.0 so the Owner's installed codex-cli 0.147.0 is in-range — the bump\n# that unblocks the PLAN-174 W2 wire (the pair-rail rounds since S317 already\n# ran on the 0.147.0 binary, advisory). LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at >=0.128.0\n# (same widen-upper-only shape as S269: executed OUTSIDE any open release\n# window — GA v1.3.0 was cut 2026-08-17 and no rc is in flight). The ADR-182\n# payload manifest (codex-cli-pin-manifes