ced the verdict — so before these bytes land no verdict\n# declaring 0.156.1 validates; step 15's optional mode\n# (CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1, a repository variable unset on\n# 2026-09-23) goes beyond tolerating a failed validation: it also skips a\n# missing verdict file and drops the parent-SHA bind; the delta+ancestry\n# gate that follows it fails closed in that mode. Landing\n# these bytes before the tag would instead break the GA's own step 15\n# (inputs_hash and payload pin both change under a verdict produced on\n# 0.155.0). Corpus rule: ADR-111 §2, restated as ADR-182 §5 step 5 (the\n# `§pin-update-protocol` label above names no heading in ADR-111) — a CLI\n# bump reopens the corpus only on a MEASURED catch_rate shift >5pp. No\n# locked-corpus run was taken for this bump (the runner's default corpus path\n# is absent from this repository and its per-fixture review is still a stub),\n# so the trigger is unevaluated, not passed. The ADR-161 per-bump checklist is\n# deferred to the substrate wave, as declared in S356 (which recorded the S352\n# re-pin as the same posture): it re-certifies Codex as a HOOK HOST, while\n# what forces this re-pin is Codex as the rail REVIEWER. DECLARED CONSEQUENCE\n# of that deferral: the installer's Codex-harness version-skew warning\n# (scripts/_codex_harness.sh) reads this same range, so widening it admits\n# 0.156.x as in-range for Codex as a hook host while the hook evidence stays\n# at 0.139.0 — a re-certification this deferral knowingly waives (every\n# widening since that reader landed, on 2026-07-10, had the same effect).\n# From 0.155.0 to 0.156.0 the exec crate's output-shape change is confined to\n# web-search items of the `codex exec --json` stream, which has no reader in\n# live code (the live rail runs `exec -o` without `--json`, and the one parser\n# of that stream in the tracked tree outside .claude/plans/ has no caller\n# outside tests; the ADR-161 live-fire procedures under .claude/plans/PLAN-155/\n# do re