{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DMfuxsa8eWSyRBkEkV6tJn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tPayload 28/32: no P0 or false declared condition established.\n2\t\n3\tNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n4\tNo new P1 findings.\n5\t\n6\tP2 follow-ups\n7\t\n8\tP2 — .claude/scripts/check-substrate-drift.py:571\n9\tThe compatibility branch accepts installed 0.139.0 against the live >=0.128.0 range, despite the manifest pinning 0.160.0. It removes the downgrade warning and remediation while the actual verifier rejects that version. Minimal fix: require the installed version to exceed the manifest version and meet the canonical compatibility floor.\n10\t\n11\tP2 — .claude/scripts/check-substrate-watch.py:238\n12\tThe floor exemption includes codex_harness, suppressing its outstanding fixture-reconciliation alert. The ledger deliberately retains 0.139.0 pending fixture rerecording; installed 0.160.0 now clears drift and omits the runbook. Minimal fix: preserve harness reconciliation drift independently of CLI version compatibility.\n13\t\n14\tP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_installer_write_safety/__init__.py:36\n15\tClass cloning retains original bases: the exported Incomplete no longer subclasses the exported ParseError, confirmed by import. Consequently, incomplete syntax reaching handlers such as _subst_commands escapes their ParseError catch and aborts the census instead of producing a blocking parse site. Minimal fix: preserve class identity or remap cloned bases consistently. Also rebind property accessors so legacy patch points remain effective.\n16\t\n17\tP2 — .claude/scripts/check-subprocess-tests.py:16\n18\tThe new installed checker requires subprocess-test-baseline.json, but install_scripts_selective() delivers only .sh/.py/.yaml siblings. Default invocation after installation therefore exits 2 because its baseline is missing. Minimal fix: install the required baseline explicitly or exclude this maintenance-only checker from adopter installations.\n19\t\n20\tP2 — .claude/scripts/check-subprocess-tests.py:21\n21\tAn explicit nonexistent --root returns success with zero findings, silently disabling the census after a CI path typo. Minimal fix: validate that the requested root exists and is a directory before scanning.\n22\t\n23\tValidation: Python 3.9 imports succeeded. The installer census completed on available files with no new blocking sites; withheld files prevent a complete baseline verdict. Full subprocess scanning was limited by redacted test syntax. No files modified.\n24\t\n25\tVERDICT: GO-WITH-CONDITIONS No declared condition is falsified by this payload and no P0 was found, while five P2 defects remain for follow-up.\n26\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9f21750-77cd-44a8-9a48-5376b7294476","uuid":"99af7db9-4faa-43ce-a6a0-14d36f43a230","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:00:47.167Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/codex-rc1-28.verdict.txt","content":"Payload 28/32: no P0 or false declared condition established.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\nNo new P1 findings.\n\nP2 follow-ups\n\nP2 — .claude/scripts/check-substrate-drift.py:571\nThe compatibility branch accepts installed 0.139.0 against the live >=0.128.0 range, despite the manifest pinning 0.160.0. It removes the downgrade warning and remediation while the actual verifier rejects that version. Minimal fix: require the installed version to exceed the manifest version and meet the canonical compatibility floor.\n\nP2 — .claude/scripts/check-substrate-watch.py:238\nThe floor exemption includes codex_harness, suppressing its outstanding fixture-reconciliation alert. The ledger deliberately retains 0.139.0 pending fixture rerecording; installed 0.160.0 now clears drift and omits the runbook. Minimal fix: preserve harness reconciliation drift independently of CLI version compatibility.\n\nP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_installer_write_safety/__init__.py:36\nClass cloning retains original bases: the exported Incomplete no longer subclasses the exported ParseError, confirmed by import. Consequently, incomplete syntax reaching handlers such as _subst_commands escapes their ParseError catch and aborts the census instead of producing a blocking parse site. Minimal fix: preserve class identity or remap cloned bases consistently. Also rebind property accessors so legacy patch points remain effective.\n\nP2 — .claude/scripts/check-subprocess-tests.py:16\nThe new installed checker requires subprocess-test-baseline.json, but install_scripts_selective() delivers only .sh/.py/.yaml siblings. Default invocation after installation therefore exits 2 because its baseline is missing. Minimal fix: install the required baseline explicitly or exclude this maintenance-only checker from adopter installations.\n\nP2 — .claude/scripts/check-subprocess-tests.py:21\nAn explicit nonexistent --root returns success with zero findings, silently disabling the census after a CI path typo. Minimal fix: validate that the requested root exists and is a directory before scanning.\n\nValidation: Python 3.9 imports succeeded. The installer census completed on available files with no new blocking sites; withheld files prevent a complete baseline verdict. Full subprocess scanning was limited by redacted test syntax. No files modified.\n\nVERDICT: GO-WITH-CONDITIONS No declared condition is falsified by this payload and no P0 was found, while five P2 defects remain for follow-up.\n","numLines":26,"startLine":1,"totalLines":26}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DMfuxsa8eWSyRBkEkV6tJn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
