{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RhvbxMLRxeTZkXaZ9Jnsg1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"check-substrate-drift.py — fast-lane substrate drift detector (lane C2).\n3\t\n4\tAnswers, OFFLINE by default, the three questions whose late answers cost the\n5\tframework days of latency. Measured: Claude Fable 5.1 launched 2026-09-01; the\n6\tframework adopted it explicitly in ``ab56e76`` (2026-09-02) and shipped that\n7\tadoption with v1.4.0 on 2026-09-15. ``@openai/codex`` 0.155.1 was published to\n8\tnpm on 2026-09-18 and first noticed on 2026-09-22.\n9\t\n10\t  1. CODEX — is the INSTALLED ``@openai/codex`` the version the ADR-182\n11\t     payload manifest pins (``.claude/governance/codex-cli-pin-manifest.json``\n12\t     ``package_version``)? A different version means the pair-rail's payload\n13\t     sha256 check will not match and ``check_pair_rail.py --verify-codex-pin``\n14\t     fails CLOSED at the next L3+ call. The installed version is READ, never\n15\t     probed: the binary is not executed (ADR-182 M4 — an unverified payload is\n16\t     never exec'd, ``pair-rail-gate.sh`` Gate 3a), and the drift case is\n17\t     exactly the unverified one. The launcher found on ``$PATH`` is resolved\n18\t     the way ``check_pair_rail._resolve_codex_payload`` resolves it\n19\t     (``<pkg>/bin/<launcher>`` -> ``<pkg>``); the version comes from the\n20\t     payload package ``@openai/codex-<os>-<cpu>/package.json``\n21\t     (``<version>-<os>-<cpu>``), else from ``<pkg>/package.json``. With a\n22\t     cached ``--fetch`` result it also answers: has npm ``@openai/codex``\n23\t     ``latest`` moved PAST the pin? No cache, or a cache older than\n24\t     ``--max-cache-age-days``, is a named ``unknown`` (never a silent\n25\t     \"current\"). This check compares VERSION STRINGS only; it never hashes\n26\t     the payload. An install whose version equals the pin but whose bytes\n27\t     differ reads as no finding here, while ``check_pair_rail.py\n28\t     --verify-codex-pin`` (the payload sha256 gate) says ``mismatch``. So a\n29\t     codex result with no finding is not \"pair-rail verified\"; the report's\n30\t     codex line and component say so (``_CODEX_VERSION_ONLY``).\n31\t  2. CLAUDE CODE — does the installed ``claude --version`` differ from the\n32\t     version the substrate ledger (``.claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json``,\n33\t     component ``claude_code``) was last reconciled against?\n34\t  3. MODELS — which model ids does the INSTALLED Claude Code know that the\n35\t     ADR-149 ``AVAILABLE_MODELS_WORKING_SET`` does not cover?\n36\t\n37\tModel catalog source (declared honestly). Claude Code (measured on 2.1.280,\n38\tthe darwin-arm64 build, 2026-09-22) exposes NO documented listing surface:\n39\t``claude --help`` lists no models subcommand and the settings ``model`` key\n40\tis a free string. The installed binary does, however, embed a structured"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9f21750-77cd-44a8-9a48-5376b7294476","uuid":"8c118a94-1337-47a0-b2fc-f7e8d9503203","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:02:38.829Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/scripts/check-substrate-drift.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"check-substrate-drift.py — fast-lane substrate drift detector (lane C2).\n\nAnswers, OFFLINE by default, the three questions whose late answers cost the\nframework days of latency. Measured: Claude Fable 5.1 launched 2026-09-01; the\nframework adopted it explicitly in ``ab56e76`` (2026-09-02) and shipped that\nadoption with v1.4.0 on 2026-09-15. ``@openai/codex`` 0.155.1 was published to\nnpm on 2026-09-18 and first noticed on 2026-09-22.\n\n  1. CODEX — is the INSTALLED ``@openai/codex`` the version the ADR-182\n     payload manifest pins (``.claude/governance/codex-cli-pin-manifest.json``\n     ``package_version``)? A different version means the pair-rail's payload\n     sha256 check will not match and ``check_pair_rail.py --verify-codex-pin``\n     fails CLOSED at the next L3+ call. The installed version is READ, never\n     probed: the binary is not executed (ADR-182 M4 — an unverified payload is\n     never exec'd, ``pair-rail-gate.sh`` Gate 3a), and the drift case is\n     exactly the unverified one. The launcher found on ``$PATH`` is resolved\n     the way ``check_pair_rail._resolve_codex_payload`` resolves it\n     (``<pkg>/bin/<launcher>`` -> ``<pkg>``); the version comes from the\n     payload package ``@openai/codex-<os>-<cpu>/package.json``\n     (``<version>-<os>-<cpu>``), else from ``<pkg>/package.json``. With a\n     cached ``--fetch`` result it also answers: has npm ``@openai/codex``\n     ``latest`` moved PAST the pin? No cache, or a cache older than\n     ``--max-cache-age-days``, is a named ``unknown`` (never a silent\n     \"current\"). This check compares VERSION STRINGS only; it never hashes\n     the payload. An install whose version equals the pin but whose bytes\n     differ reads as no finding here, while ``check_pair_rail.py\n     --verify-codex-pin`` (the payload sha256 gate) says ``mismatch``. So a\n     codex result with no finding is not \"pair-rail verified\"; the report's\n     codex line and component say so (``_CODEX_VERSION_ONLY``).\n  2. CLAUDE CODE — does the installed ``claude --version`` differ from the\n     version the substrate ledger (``.claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json``,\n     component ``claude_code``) was last reconciled against?\n  3. MODELS — which model ids does the INSTALLED Claude Code know that the\n     ADR-149 ``AVAILABLE_MODELS_WORKING_SET`` does not cover?\n\nModel catalog source (declared honestly). Claude Code (measured on 2.1.280,\nthe darwin-arm64 build, 2026-09-22) exposes NO documented listing surface:\n``claude --help`` lists no models subcommand and the settings ``model`` key\nis a free string. The installed binary does, 